Configuration coverage
Strings and string_view inputs share a single direct read_json<T>(string_view) boundary.
Files are read into strings, checked for I/O errors and passed to that same parsing path.
Unknown keys are ignored while their values are fully syntactically validated.
Required fields, defaults, UTF-8 checks and complete trailing-content rejection are covered.
A configuration with a 100,000-byte token and 100,000 bytes of trailing whitespace succeeds;
non-whitespace content after that tail fails. No streaming-window token limit applies.
Native checked integer conversion accepts exact positive exponent forms in settings.
Fractional values, numeric overflow, booleans and invalid durations are rejected.
Glaze's native integer conversion rejects decimal-point and negative-exponent spellings;
no custom integer-token wrapper or lexical classification policy is added.
Maximum size_t counts remain intact. Module-owned validate overloads run in order:
symbols, feed, window and output; Result::and_then stops at the first failure.
Windows accept 1 second through 365 days in JSON and direct construction.
Repeated valid keys use their last value; repeated sections replace complete earlier sections.
Invalid earlier known fields fail immediately instead of being discarded before conversion.
Config, feed, statistics and output keep native mappings in their own json_meta.hpp files.
Glaze error_ctx diagnostics become Result errors only at the shared parsing boundary.

Ticker JSON adapter coverage
Framed string_view input is parsed without a stream adapter or message copy.
A view ending before nonterminating bytes succeeds without reading those bytes.
TickerUpdate, Price and Timestamp hooks preserve exact prices, maximum uint64 IDs,
control-message filtering, escaped text and detailed typed domain errors.
Positive-exponent IDs are exact, including 1844674407370955161e1 near the uint64 limit.
Negative, fractional, overflowing and malformed IDs fail; unused malformed fields and
trailing root content fail. Off-grid prices retain their OutOfRange category.

Numeric coverage
16,000 randomized window updates match an independent sorted exact reference.
1,000 generated integer prices parse from decimal/scientific text and format exactly.
Boundary cases cover the maximum price, off-grid input, sums beyond uint64,
expiration of maximum prices, fractional means/medians, half-even ties and output carry.
The independent verifier accepts the specified ties and rejects incorrect rounding/off-grid prices.

